;; The words a predictor's signature wraps around its fields (RFC-005):
;; brainyard's clj-llm prompt (`json-schema-instruction`, the field lists, the
;; objective line, render-demos), the same for every predictor. Read by the
;; model, so a resource (RFC-001); signature.clj fills each {name} in one pass,
;; so a filled-in value is never read for names again (byj-2e8.4).
;;
;; {schema} the reply's JSON Schema; {skeleton} the reply's shape with
;; <placeholders>; {fields} the numbered field list, or, in :user-tail, the
;; output fields in order joined by :field-sep; {instructions} the predictor's
;; own; {examples} the rendered :demo of each, a blank line apart; {n} {inputs}
;; {output} one demonstration.
{:reasoning-desc "Brief reasoning leading to the answer: at most 3 short sentences (~60 words). Plain prose only; no headings, no bullet lists, no code blocks. State the decision and why; do not restate the inputs, narrate what you are about to do, or explain the output format."
 :input-fields "Your input fields are:
{fields}"
 :output-fields "Your output fields are:
{fields}"
 :response-format "## Response format
Reply with a single JSON object that IS your answer. The JSON Schema below describes that object's shape: the top level of your reply is the object itself, never the schema.

JSON Schema:
{schema}

Shape of your reply — each <placeholder> stands for a value of that type (numbers and booleans unquoted):
{skeleton}

A field you have nothing for stays empty: an empty string is written \"\" (not \"\\\"\\\"\"), an empty array []. Output only the JSON object: no text before or after it, no markdown fences. Use exactly the field names shown."
 :respond-all "Respond with a JSON object containing all output fields."
 :respond "Respond with a JSON object containing the output fields."
 :demos "Here are examples of inputs and the JSON object to respond with:

{examples}"
 :demo "Example {n}
Input:
{inputs}
Output:
{output}"
 :objective "In adhering to this structure, your objective is:
{instructions}"
 :user-tail "Respond with a JSON object containing the output fields, starting with the field {fields}."
 :field-sep ", then "}
